1. Origin: OpenUUYC

Farwing is derived from OpenUUYC by djkcyl and contributors
(https://github.com/djkcyl/openuuyc, v1.0.0-rc.3, commit 506df56). The
original OpenUUYC copyright, provenance and license notice is preserved
verbatim in licenses/OpenUUYC-NOTICE.txt. Mentions of "OpenUUYC" below
describe that history.

OpenUUYC implemented interoperability with the NetEase UU Remote service.
Farwing removes that service binding: it uses its own Farwing Protocol
(docs/protocol/farwing-protocol.md) and the self-hosted Farwing Server, and
does not contact, load or require any UU Remote service, client, SDK,
credential or component. The names UU Remote and NetEase, and their code,
documentation, marks, assets and services, belong to their respective
rightsholders; Farwing claims no affiliation.

Parameter provenance: OpenUUYC's notice stated that its RS-FEC repair-count
tables (formerly src/features/host/fec-high-rtt.bin and fec-low-rtt.bin)
were obtained from the UU V4.7.3 SDK. Farwing deleted those tables; repair
counts are now computed from a binomial loss model in
src/transport/fec_policy.rs. The same notice listed the bitrate budget
table in src/features/host/parameters.rs; it is retained unchanged in this
release to preserve streaming behavior and is scheduled for review.

